1. Ownership and Copyright

All software, source code, website designs, applications, projects, documentation, graphics, and related materials developed, owned, or legally assigned to Adeeb Technology Lab are protected by applicable copyright and intellectual property laws.

2. No Unauthorized Use

No individual, organization, or third party may use, copy, modify, reproduce, sell, distribute, publish, or commercially exploit any part of the Company's proprietary projects without prior written permission from Adeeb Technology Lab.

3. Student and Intern Contributions

Students and interns may access and work with project source code strictly for their assigned internship or development responsibilities.

Contributing to a project does not automatically grant ownership or unrestricted usage rights. Ownership of contributions shall be determined by the applicable signed Student Internship and Intellectual Property Agreement and applicable law.

4. Portfolio and Public Display

Students may reference publicly available projects on their GitHub profiles and portfolios for professional demonstration and job applications, provided they do not claim ownership of the Company's intellectual property or independently reuse, distribute, or republish the source code without written authorization.

5. Restrictions After Internship Completion

After completing or leaving an internship or working relationship, students and interns must not independently reuse, modify, publish, distribute, sell, or commercially exploit Company-owned source code or projects without obtaining prior written permission from Adeeb Technology Lab.

6. Authorized Third Parties

Individuals or organizations who receive written authorization from Adeeb Technology Lab may use, modify, upload, distribute, or share the specified project only within the scope of the permission granted.

Permission granted to one individual or organization cannot automatically be transferred to another party.

7. Unauthorized Copying and Redistribution

Unauthorized copying, downloading for reuse, modification, uploading, republishing, redistribution, resale, or commercial use of Company-owned copyrighted materials is prohibited, except for rights expressly granted by applicable law or GitHub's platform terms.

8. Repeat Infringement and Unauthorized Redistribution

Any repeated unauthorized copying, uploading, redistribution, or commercial use of the Company's copyrighted software or source code may result in further copyright complaints, platform takedown requests, legal notices, and appropriate legal action under applicable laws.

9. Copyright Protection and Enforcement

Adeeb Technology Lab reserves the right, where legally entitled, to submit copyright infringement complaints, request removal of unauthorized content, and pursue available legal remedies against individuals or organizations violating these terms.

10. No Transfer of Ownership

Viewing or accessing a public repository does not transfer ownership or grant any general license to use, reproduce, modify, or distribute the Company's proprietary software.

11. Third-Party Materials

Third-party libraries, frameworks, tools, and components included in a project remain subject to their respective licenses and copyright terms. This license does not override third-party licensing rights.

12. Applicable Law

This license shall be interpreted in accordance with applicable laws of Pakistan, subject to any mandatory legal requirements.

